## 0. What this run had to settle

RESEARCH A1 — whether the connecting role can INSERT into `public.compute_job_kinds`
on HOSTED TEST — is the one thing the self-test lane CANNOT prove: the lane's
`postgres` is initdb's SUPERUSER, so `rolsuper` is always true there and the
BYPASSRLS assertion can be satisfied but never falsified. `public.compute_job_kinds`
carries FORCE ROW LEVEL SECURITY (supabase/schema/baseline.sql:9578) and its ONLY
policy is SELECT-only (`compute_job_kinds_read`, :13012), so FORCE removes the owner
exemption and an INSERT without BYPASSRLS aborts with 42501. Only a full transaction
against hosted TEST measures it. That is what `--mode preflight` is for.

